    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Consider the polynomial function \\(p\\) given by \\(p(x)=5x^3+6x^2+4x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Evaluate the function at \\(x=\\text-5\\) and \\(x=15\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "How does knowing that \\(5,\\!000+600+40 = 5,\\!640\\) help you solve the equation \\(5x^3+6x^2+4x=5,\\!640\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(11^2 = 121\\) and \\((x+1)^2 = x^2 + 2x +1\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(11^3 = 1331\\) while \\((x+1)^3 = x^3 + 3x^2 + 3x + 1\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The digits in the powers of 11 correspond to the coefficients of the polynomials.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Is this still true for \\(11^4\\) and \\((x+1)^4\\)? What about \\(11^5\\) and \\((x+1)^5\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "2.2: Polynomials in the Integers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Give a mathematical justification of Han’s observation.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "At the end of 12th grade, Clare’s aunt started investing money for her to use after graduating from college four years later. The first deposit was \\$300. If \\(r\\) is the annual interest rate of the account, then at the end of each school…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "After one year, the total value is \\(300x\\). After two years, the total value is \\(300x \\boldcdot x = 300x^2\\). Write an expression for the total value after graduation in terms of \\(x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If Clare’s aunt had invested another \\$500 at the end of her freshman year, what would the expression be for the total value after graduation in terms of \\(x\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Pause here for a whole-class discussion.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Suppose that \\$250 was invested at the end of sophomore year, and \\$400 at the end of junior year in addition to the original \\$300 and the \\$500 invested at the end of freshman year. Write an expression for the total value after…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The total amount \\(y\\), in dollars, after four years is a function \\(y=C(x)\\) of the growth factor \\(x\\). If the total Clare receives after graduation is \\(C(x)=1,\\!580\\), use a graph to find the interest rate that the account earned.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Let’s say we’re going to invest \\$200 at an annual interest rate of \\(r\\). This means at the end of a year, the balance in the account is multiplied by a growth factor of \\(x=1+r\\). After the first year, the amount in the account can be…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If an additional \\$350 is invested at the end of the first year, we can revise the polynomial. The amount of money in the account after 1 year is the same, but now the amount of money after two years is \\((200x + 350)x=200x^2+350x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What will the polynomial expression look like if \\$400 more is invested at the end of the second year and \\$150 more is invested at the end of the third year? \\(200x^4 + 350x^3 + 400x^2 +150x\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Let \\(D(x)\\) be the amount of money in dollars in the account after four years and \\(x\\) be the growth factor where \\(D(x) =200x^4 + 350x^3 + 400x^2 +150x\\). A graph of \\(y=D(x)\\) helps us visualize how the amount in the account after four…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can use this polynomial model to examine the effect of different annual interest rates, or to estimate what the annual interest rate needs to be to achieve a specific quantity at the end of the four years. For example, point A is at…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Polynomial models are adaptable to a variety of situations even as they grow in complexity.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U02-L02-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "2.3: A Yearly Gift",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A polynomial function of \\(x\\) is a function given by a sum of terms, each of which is a constant times a whole number power of \\(x\\). The word polynomial is used to refer both to the function and to the expression defining it.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u02-l02.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
